LoRA Witness implementation, tests and synthetic fixture weights are original.
The runtime requires NumPy (BSD-3-Clause, with additional notices in its wheel),
safetensors (Apache-2.0) and threadpoolctl (BSD-3-Clause). Each dependency is
installed separately and retains its own license and notices.

The optional oracle uses Kohya sd-scripts (Apache-2.0), Diffusers (Apache-2.0),
PEFT (Apache-2.0), Transformers (Apache-2.0), Accelerate (Apache-2.0), PyTorch
and torchvision (BSD-style licenses), and the Stability AI SDXL Base UNet
configuration (model repository marked OpenRAIL++). Oracle setup retrieves
upstream files at pinned revisions for local use. This distribution contains
no upstream source, model configuration, or pretrained weights.
